    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0750" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.311D1/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-28T11:00:00+01:00">April 28, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 28—8:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>124. Your 107, April 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d500-f1"/> Ferguson says
                    that no agenda has been prepared for proposed Conference. In effect the
                    Conference is simply a gathering of the representatives of the wheat exporting
                    countries to discuss whether or not in the present situation it is worthwhile to
                    try to form some plan for the betterment of wheat market and if so what.</p>
                <p>Ferguson will give me for transmission a full list of those who have accepted
                    invitations within a few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
